KG42.register("slice-clusters-81cef7a1f5136e625f55622c",{"id":"17-exogenous_cost_allocation::v142-d-K001","paper":"17-exogenous_cost_allocation","title":"Decentralized quantity-price negotiation given exogenous network charges and participation conditions","source_pointer":"/clusters/67","node_ids":["COMP-b9841ac99d9d29b8","COMP-166b347ab5fcd2a9","COMP-486b93e7e3eb4336","COMP-b3f649e90c1f17b9","COMP-f01e7a521b5470f4","COMP-a774da994c2ca212","COMP-4fd16cbd90d234cb"],"rule_refs":["17-exogenous_cost_allocation::v141-c-R001","17-exogenous_cost_allocation::v141-c-R002","17-exogenous_cost_allocation::v141-c-R003","17-exogenous_cost_allocation::v141-c-R004","17-exogenous_cost_allocation::v141-c-R006","17-exogenous_cost_allocation::v141-c-R007","17-exogenous_cost_allocation::v141-c-R005"],"visible_rule_refs":["17-exogenous_cost_allocation::v141-c-R001","17-exogenous_cost_allocation::v141-c-R002","17-exogenous_cost_allocation::v141-c-R003","17-exogenous_cost_allocation::v141-c-R004","17-exogenous_cost_allocation::v141-c-R006","17-exogenous_cost_allocation::v141-c-R007","17-exogenous_cost_allocation::v141-c-R005"],"suppressed_rule_refs":[],"edges":[{"global_edge_id":"S-c7b4dc58195c2296","source":"COMP-166b347ab5fcd2a9","target":"COMP-b9841ac99d9d29b8","type":"links","assertion_ids":["17-exogenous_cost_allocation::v141-c-R001::E::v141-c-R001-E001"],"rule_refs":["17-exogenous_cost_allocation::v141-c-R001"],"internal":false},{"global_edge_id":"S-75b92d2aa919eef0","source":"COMP-486b93e7e3eb4336","target":"COMP-b9841ac99d9d29b8","type":"limits","assertion_ids":["17-exogenous_cost_allocation::v141-c-R001::E::v141-c-R001-E002"],"rule_refs":["17-exogenous_cost_allocation::v141-c-R001"],"internal":false},{"global_edge_id":"S-7d6be3efa52b74fc","source":"COMP-b9841ac99d9d29b8","target":"COMP-b3f649e90c1f17b9","type":"links","assertion_ids":["17-exogenous_cost_allocation::v141-c-R002::E::v141-c-R002-E001"],"rule_refs":["17-exogenous_cost_allocation::v141-c-R002"],"internal":false},{"global_edge_id":"S-863884eb83fcc2a1","source":"COMP-166b347ab5fcd2a9","target":"COMP-b3f649e90c1f17b9","type":"links","assertion_ids":["17-exogenous_cost_allocation::v141-c-R002::E::v141-c-R002-E002"],"rule_refs":["17-exogenous_cost_allocation::v141-c-R002"],"internal":false},{"global_edge_id":"S-809135306b16ee45","source":"COMP-486b93e7e3eb4336","target":"COMP-b3f649e90c1f17b9","type":"limits","assertion_ids":["17-exogenous_cost_allocation::v141-c-R002::E::v141-c-R002-E003"],"rule_refs":["17-exogenous_cost_allocation::v141-c-R002"],"internal":false},{"global_edge_id":"S-1c8733484f5fc703","source":"COMP-166b347ab5fcd2a9","target":"COMP-f01e7a521b5470f4","type":"links","assertion_ids":["17-exogenous_cost_allocation::v141-c-R003::E::v141-c-R003-E001"],"rule_refs":["17-exogenous_cost_allocation::v141-c-R003"],"internal":false},{"global_edge_id":"S-b960eee1283d0d94","source":"COMP-b9841ac99d9d29b8","target":"COMP-166b347ab5fcd2a9","type":"links","assertion_ids":["17-exogenous_cost_allocation::v141-c-R004::E::v141-c-R004-E001"],"rule_refs":["17-exogenous_cost_allocation::v141-c-R004"],"internal":false},{"global_edge_id":"S-c6ee6885678aabaf","source":"COMP-b3f649e90c1f17b9","target":"COMP-166b347ab5fcd2a9","type":"links","assertion_ids":["17-exogenous_cost_allocation::v141-c-R004::E::v141-c-R004-E002"],"rule_refs":["17-exogenous_cost_allocation::v141-c-R004"],"internal":false},{"global_edge_id":"S-bdced9f4178cba6b","source":"COMP-166b347ab5fcd2a9","target":"COMP-486b93e7e3eb4336","type":"links","assertion_ids":["17-exogenous_cost_allocation::v141-c-R005::E::v141-c-R005-E001"],"rule_refs":["17-exogenous_cost_allocation::v141-c-R005"],"internal":false}],"unresolved_rule_refs":[],"interface_annotations":[{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-CN001","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R003","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C001","v141-c-R003::phi::v141-c-R003-C003"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C005"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e13","v141-b-g01-e14","v141-b-g01-e17","v141-b-g01-e18"],"rationale":"The source explicitly solves Equation (5) by Equation (6), and the local objective carries separable costs and network charges; this correspondence applies only to the exogenous objective, and the endogenous reference objective is not connected to the same solution."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-CN002","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C003","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C004","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C006"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C004","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C007"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e10","v141-b-g01-e17","v141-b-g01-e20"],"rationale":"The two chains describe the same signed local optimization and sending action by buy/sell function and retain role restrictions separately; they are not interpreted as two independent optimization programs, first demand and then supply."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-CN003","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::p_nm","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C003"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-theta-p-mn-k","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e17","v141-b-g01-e20"],"rationale":"When a request comes from a counterparty, the previous-round request after swapping the agent index enters the local update of this agent. This interface retains historical iterations and reverse transaction pairs, and does not treat the two sides' not-yet-converged proposals as equal or as negatives of each other."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-CN004","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R002::x::v141-c-R002-x-p-nm","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C004"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-x-p-nm","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C001","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C006"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e17","v141-b-g01-e19","v141-b-g01-e20"],"rationale":"The updated and exchanged supply-side proposal is the quantity input for this round's price and residual calculation; the condition of receiving all counter-proposals comes from the source-stated procedure, and the specific interpretation of the residual remains a gap."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-CN005","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R001::x::p_nm","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C003"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-x-p-nm","v141-c-R004::phi::v141-c-R004-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e10","v141-b-g01-e17","v141-b-g01-e20"],"rationale":"The request-side counter-proposal enters the same bilateral price update, with applicability conditions being receipt of the request and all partner counter-proposals; a separate request-price algorithm is not established."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-CN006","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","kind":"quantity_interface","from_refs":["v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-x-lambda-nm"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-theta-lambda-nm-k","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e17","v141-b-g01-e18","v141-b-g01-e20"],"rationale":"The bilateral price produced by coordination serves as a known iteration input in subsequent local optimization; its roles as a decision variable and as a local parameter in the two chains are retained separately."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-CN007","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R004","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","kind":"functional_coupling","from_refs":["v141-c-R004::x::v141-c-R004-x-lambda-nm"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C002"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e17","v141-b-g01-e20"],"rationale":"The same negotiated price feedback also acts on the request-side update; R001 retains the procedural statement, and the complete local objective is referenced through R002, without supplementing additional formulas."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-CN008","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-theta002","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C004","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C005"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R001::theta::omega_n","v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C001"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e09","v141-b-g01-e15","v141-b-g01-e20"],"rationale":"The partner permission set limits which transaction pairs a request may be directed to; tradability is not equivalent to mandatory execution, and exit remains constrained by the source's power-bound conditions."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-CN009","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R005","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R005::theta::v141-c-R005-theta002","v141-c-R005::phi::v141-c-R005-C004"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R002::theta::v141-c-R002-theta-omega-n","v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C003"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e09","v141-b-g01-e17","v141-b-g01-e20"],"rationale":"Supply proposals are likewise limited by the partner permission scope; this is a common feasible-region condition, not a procedure in which network charges automatically change the partner set."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-CN010","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R006","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R002","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R006::phi::v141-c-R006-C001"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R002::phi::v141-c-R002-C007"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e10","v141-b-g01-e14","v141-b-g01-e17"],"rationale":"The consumer role constraint maintains the same non-selling condition in Equation (5) and in the local update, and the participation rule and submission rule jointly delimit the consumer decision."},{"connection_id":"v142-d-K001-CN011","from_chain_id":"v141-c-R007","to_chain_id":"v141-c-R001","kind":"complementary_scope","from_refs":["v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C002","v141-c-R007::phi::v141-c-R007-C003"],"to_refs":["v141-c-R001::phi::v141-c-R001-C005"],"evidence_ids":["v141-b-g01-e10","v141-b-g01-e17"],"rationale":"The prosumer zero-crossing boundary explains its bidirectional trading eligibility, while the bilateral boundary enters the request update; this condition applies only to prosumers and cannot be generalized to consumers or generators."}],"annotation_policy":"Original D connections are annotations, not additional S edges.","empty_after_chain_suppression":false});
